A1. What do old hens do at dinner time? ~ CACKLE
A6. What should be stocked with filthy lucre? ~ LARDER
A12. What could be used to get an edge on? ~ HONE
A14. Name a King Shakespeare wrote about. ~ LEAR
A16. Which movie actress is Rich? ~ IRENE
A18. How many of the commandments are hard to keep? ~ TEN
A19. Whose country was dry before the Volstead Act? ~ ARABS
A21. What animal is known for its daming ways? ~ BEAVER
A23. What would a rain storm be in California? ~ CRISIS
A24. What is it to wait in Glasgow? ~ BIDE
A25. How are the eyes of China? ~ ASKEW
A26. What old boy was always fiddling around? ~ NERO
A27. What is half a X word printer's measure? ~ EN
A28. What do you have for the one you love? ~ YEN
A30. In what game is IT used? ~ TAG
A32. Who always buries his mistakes? (abbr.). ~ DR
A34. What is a part of the best circles? ~ ARC
A37. What kind of calf isn't so good in the long run? ~ FATTED
A38. How does Sheba feel about a spend-thrift sheik? ~ ADORES
A40. What is a 90-year-old man who wears a straw hat in January? ~ OLD
A43. What is it that even the most hard-boiled editor doesn't dare reject? ~ AD
A45. What did the old hen do for her chicks? ~ SAT
A47. What do the girls like around them? ~ ARM
A49. Name a French definite article. ~ LA
A50. What do you do when you cross the street? ~ RISK
A52. Where does the bashful farmer boy find his honey? ~ HIVES
A53. What is a portent of good or evil? ~ OMEN
A55. What is it that's hot in Mexico? ~ TAMALE
A57. What is a man of learning or science? ~ SAVANT
A59. What kind of people are supposed to travel in the best circles? ~ ELITE
A60. What boat was famed for its beastly passenger list? ~ ARK
A61. Who was the liberator of Hamelin? ~ PIPER
A62. What is it that is over the head of most sheiks? ~ TENT
A64. What do the best steppers in Scotland dance? ~ REEL
A65. What do little brothers usually do? ~ PESTER
A66. Name something often at sea. ~ VESSEL

D2. What did the horseman of Sleepy Hollow lack? ~ AHEAD
D3. What is it difficult to get a second-hand car to do? ~ CONVEY
D4. What joint is being continually exposed? ~ KNEE
D5. Name a definite article in France. ~ LE
D7. Who is a likely candidate for our next President? (init.). ~ AL
D8. What is the safest thing to guard during a military advance? ~ REAR
D9. What kind of man talks back to his wife? ~ DARING
D10. What is the wisest thing to do to your mistakes? ~ ERASE
D11. Where did undesirable persons used to hang out? ~ GIBBET
D13. What kind of a person is fond of pets? ~ NECKER
D15. What is it to separate into classes or kinds? ~ ASSORT
D17. What is it Kaiser Wilhelm "ain't going to do no more"? ~ REIN
D20. Name one kind of high flyer. ~ BIRD
D22. How did Calvin Coolidge get to Washington? ~ RAN
D23. What is the abbreviation for "hundredweight"? ~ CWT
D29. What is the Roman soldier in "Ben Hur" who carries a spear? ~ EXTRA
D31. What is love in France? ~ AMOUR
D33. What is it that you lose when you stand up? ~ LAP
D34. What was trouble to Shakespeare? ~ ADO
D35. What kind of fellow would tell on a perfectly good bootlegger? ~ CAD
D36. Without what would a Ziegfeld Revue not have a leg to stand on? ~ LEG
D39. What kind of hold-up is often seen on the avenue? ~ GARTER
D41. What people are usually in the dark? ~ LOVERS
D42. Where do most little boys get in a jam? ~ PANTRY
D44. What is it that is always on the watch? ~ DIAL
D45. What kind of slippers are worn outdoors in the winter time? ~ SKATES
D46. Name a definite article. ~ THE
D47. What is always acting like a donkey? ~ ASS
D48. What is the Sunday-go-to-meeting place of the present generation? ~ MOVIES
D49. What is a name for any smooth unaspiring consonant? ~ LENE
D51. Give another name for a sock. ~ SMITE
D54. What is the family tree of a very good sap? ~ MAPLE
D56. What is considered a fast time by some? ~ LENT
D58. What were the ancestors of people who live in Tennessee? ~ APES
D63. What is the symbol for tellurium? ~ TE
D64. Name one of the notes in the scale. ~ RE


